    {
      "id": "node_b3fdad12-aa8a-4d1f-a50c-bc43654bb903",
      "name": "socket_accept",
      "kind": "Processor",
      "parentId": "root",
      "children": [],
      "incomingLinks": [
        "992f1269-5aa2-4929-91a3-5745c23f6cb9",
        "link_47dfe6fa-791b-4863-99ff-002db0ff8f88",
        "link_559f3fef-7b5a-4d0e-9d55-8f70aa5c46b8",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "outgoingLinks": [
        "link_66e6e8e4-5fb1-4171-8bc9-1d22a4323ec5",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "x": 222.32325019058075,
        "y": 1098.441268190992,
        "width": 200.0,
        "height": 138.0,
        "closedWidth": 200.0,
        "closedHeight": 138.0,
        "openWidth": 200.0,
        "openHeight": 138.0,
        "isExpanded": true
      },
      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
      "text": {
        "source": "// Counters that a C body keeps in statics live in the run context.\n@Suppress(\"UNCHECKED_CAST\")\nval state = context.imports.getOrPut(\"socket_accept\") {\n    mutableMapOf(\n        \"sequence\" to 0L,\n        \"resolved\" to 0L,\n        \"limit\" to (System.getenv(\"WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS\")?.trim()?.toLongOrNull() ?: 0L),\n    )\n} as MutableMap<String, Long>\n// Both buffers of the awaitResponseLoop self-link hold the pending copies.\nval pending = arrayOf(awaitResponseLoop_in, awaitResponseLoop_out)\n\n// 1. Resolve every response against its pending copy, rotating each loop buffer once.\nwhile (response.isNotEmpty()) {\n    val item = response.removeFirst()\n    var found = false\n    for (side in pending) {\n        repeat(side.size) {\n            val waiting = side.removeFirst()\n            if (found || waiting.id != item.id) {\n                side.addLast(waiting)\n            } else {\n                found = true\n                if (libhttp.http_resolve(waiting, item) != 0) {\n                    System.err.println(\"webserver: client closed the connection early\")\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    if (!found) throw IllegalStateException(\"webserver: response ${item.id} has no pending request\")\n    val resolved = state.getValue(\"resolved\") + 1\n    state[\"resolved\"] = resolved\n    val limit = state.getValue(\"limit\")\n    if (limit > 0 && resolved >= limit) threadworkRunner.shutdownRequest()\n}\n// 2. Accept at most one connection; wait briefly only when nothing is in flight.\nif (threadworkRunner.isRunning()) {\n    val idle = awaitResponseLoop_in.isEmpty() && awaitResponseLoop_out.isEmpty()\n    if (libhttp.http_wait(if (idle) 25 else 0)) {\n        val sequence = state.getValue(\"sequence\") + 1\n        state[\"sequence\"] = sequence\n        val (accepted, status) = libhttp.http_accept(sequence)\n        if (status < 0) throw IllegalStateException(\"webserver: accepting a connection failed\")\n        if (accepted != null) {\n            request.addLast(accepted)\n            awaitResponseLoop_out.addLast(accepted)\n        }\n    }\n} else if (awaitResponseLoop_in.isEmpty() && awaitResponseLoop_out.isEmpty()) {\n    libhttp.http_close()\n}",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "// Like atoi, text that is not a number yields port 0, which fails to listen.\nval port = System.getenv(\"WEBSERVER_PORT\")?.let { it.trim().toIntOrNull() ?: 0 } ?: 8080\nval anyAddress = System.getenv(\"WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY\") == \"1\"\nif (libhttp.http_listen(port, anyAddress) != 0) {\n    System.err.println(\"webserver: cannot listen on port $port\")\n    throw IllegalStateException(\"webserver: cannot listen on port $port\")\n}\nprintln(\"webserver: listening on http://${if (anyAddress) \"0.0.0.0\" else \"127.0.0.1\"}:$port\")\nSystem.out.flush()",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "Entry and exit point of every request.\n\nInitialization: read WEBSERVER_PORT and WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY, open the listener with\nlibhttp.http_listen and print \"webserver: listening on http://<address>:<port>\".\nFailure to listen is an error (the process exits non-zero).\n\nEach tick:\n1. Pop every resolved ReqRep from `response` and find its pending copy by id in the\n   awaitResponseLoop self-link. Both of its buffers (awaitResponseLoop_in and\n   awaitResponseLoop_out) are searched by rotating each once, so the copies that do not\n   match keep their order. Resolve the match with libhttp.http_resolve (write the reply,\n   log it, close, free). A response without a pending copy is an error.\n2. While running, accept at most one connection with libhttp.http_accept and push the new\n   ReqRep to both `request` (router) and awaitResponseLoop_out (pending copy). Wait up to\n   25 ms for a connection only when nothing is pending.\n3. Count resolutions; at WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS request shutdown.\nAfter shutdown, stop accepting and close the listener once nothing is pending.",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "- With an unused port, startup prints the listening URL and the process keeps running.\n- With the port already in use, initialization fails and the process exits non-zero.\n- Two concurrent clients receive the responses matching their own requests (ids differ).\n- WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS=1 exits 0 after exactly one access-log line.",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
      "binaryContent": null,
